Netscape Navigator 5.0b1 for IRIX
=================================

The browser from the 1998 Mozilla Classic source release (the tree that
would have become Netscape Communicator 5.0), ported to IRIX 6.5 with
today's compilers, with TLS (HTTPS) from OpenSSL in place of the security
code the source release left out.  Browser only: no mail, news or editor.

Run:     /usr/local/bin/netscape5 [URL]
Needs:   IRIX 6.5.22 or later, X11 and IRIX's Motif (x_eoe, motif_eoe);
         any MIPS CPU.  Nothing else: every library it uses besides IRIX's
         is linked into the program.
Fonts:   page text is drawn by FreeType in Arimo, Tinos and Cousine (the
         Chrome OS core fonts, metric-compatible with Arial, Times New
         Roman and Courier New), with DejaVu Sans for what they lack:
         /usr/local/lib/netscape5/fonts (NS_FONT_DIR names another).
HTTP/2:  used with servers that offer it (over TLS); NS_HTTP2=0 turns it
         off.
Trusts:  the Mozilla root certificates in /usr/local/lib/netscape5/cacert.pem
         (also OpenSSL's default store, SSL_CERT_FILE and SSL_CERT_DIR).
X class: Netscape5 (so it keeps clear of Netscape 4's app-defaults/Netscape).
Profile: ~/.netscape5 (Netscape 4 keeps ~/.netscape; the two do not mix).

Debugging: NETSCAPE_NET_DEBUG=1 logs TLS handshakes and network errors.

Source, and how it was built: https://github.com/atomchild411/netscape
(branch irix).  pkgsrc users: www/netscape5 in
https://github.com/atomchild411/pkgsrc (branch irix).

Licenses: licenses/ -- the Netscape Public License 1.0 for Navigator;
OpenSSL (Apache License 2.0) and LLVM's libc++ (Apache License 2.0 with
LLVM exception) are linked in, as are QuickJS (JavaScript), NetSurf's
libcss, libdom, libhubbub, libparserutils and libwapcaplet (style sheets
and the DOM), all MIT licence, nanosvg (SVG images, zlib licence),
libpng (PNG Reference Library licence), libjpeg-turbo (IJG, BSD and zlib
licences), zlib, bzip2 (BSD-style), FreeType (FreeType License), libwebp
(BSD, with Google's patent grant) and nghttp2 (HTTP/2, MIT licence).
The fonts: croscorefonts (Apache License 2.0) and DejaVu (Bitstream Vera
licence, and public domain changes).  cacert.pem is from Mozilla (MPL 2.0).
